(1. THREATS IN UNTREATED FIELD WATER: Surface water in field terrain) Tj
T*
(contains suspended colloidal silt, organic matter, and dangerous biological) Tj
T*
(pathogens responsible for cholera, amoebic dysentery, typhoid fever, and) Tj
T*
(viral hepatitis A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. THE 3-STAGE MILITARY PURIFICATION SEQUENCE: Standard military water) Tj
T*
(treatment follows a sequential 3-step doctrine: Stage 1: Clarification and) Tj
T*
(sedimentation of heavy suspended solids; Stage 2: Physical filtration) Tj
T*
(through clean sand/cloth filters; Stage 3: Chemical sterilization using) Tj
T*
(bleaching powder \(calcium hypochlorite\) or chlorination tablets \(Halazone\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. BOILING STANDARDS & CHEMICAL DOSING: When chemical reagents are) Tj
T*
(unavailable, water must be brought to a vigorous rolling boil for a minimum) Tj
T*
(of 20 continuous minutes. When using water purification tablets, one tablet) Tj
T*
(treats one liter of clear water, requiring a 30-minute contact time before) Tj
T*
(consumption, maintaining a safe residual chlorine level of 0.5 ppm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. STORAGE PROTOCOLS: Purified water must be stored in sterilized, covered) Tj
T*
(galvanised iron \(GI\) tanks or military water carts with tap dispensers,) Tj
T*
(never accessed via dipping open mugs or hands.) Tj
